== Solution ==
<!-- 
Board examination showed some liquid damage on the keyboard facing side directly under the T2 chip. PP1V8_AWAKE was shorted to ground due to some corroded caps (C4522, C4526, C4523, C4535). Also replaced C4411 (PP0V9_SLPDDR) - note this rail measures very low at around 35 ohms or so and does not indicate a fault. C4526/C4411 are a 9.1uF feed through capacitor (Murata NFM15PC915D0E3D). You can steal them off a 820-1700 donor board.

Be careful in this area as the T2 is directly on the opposite side of the board, don't know if it's underfilled or not as it's hidden under a metal shield. So I used low melt and an iron to get these caps off first before reworking with a lower melting point solder. This board did start to boot on the bench, but would then power off. Only booted when put back in the chassis with everything connected.

-->



